// M1's exit (docs/ROADMAP.md, exit criteria): a document of several pages
// typed as a person would, with headings, bold and italic, in Latin, Greek,
// Cyrillic, Arabic, Hebrew and Chinese. It's undone down to an empty page,
// redone to the end, and closed and opened again. shot draws its pages
// (`exit-pages`), and crates/app/tests/sessions.rs checks that it reopens
// to the same dump and renders, and exports the same pages as a PDF.
//
// Chinese stands for CJK: M1 has no command to set a language, and the
// CJK faces draw Chinese forms where no language says otherwise.
(
    size: (900, 700),
    events: [
        Key("Primary+1"),
        Type("A walking skeleton, typed"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("This document was typed into xWorks as a person types: a key at a time, with shortcuts for its headings, its bold and its italic. Its text is stored as objects and operations, laid out in fixed-point units, shaped with HarfRust, broken into lines first fit, poured into pages of one style and drawn by the same renderer that tests use. "),
        Key("Primary+I"),
        Type("Nothing here is hand-placed."),
        Key("Primary+I"),
        Type(" When a paragraph does not fit at the foot of a page it breaks between lines, leaving at least two of them on each side, and a heading never ends a page without the start of the text it heads."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("The aim is an office suite that is "),
        Key("Primary+B"),
        Type("usable, fast and correct"),
        Key("Primary+B"),
        Type(". Usable means the program does what people expect, in the order they expect it, without asking them to learn its internals. Fast means every keystroke reaches the screen before the next one, and that opening, saving and scrolling never make anyone wait for work they did not ask for. Correct means that numbers add up exactly, that text in every script is shaped and ordered as its readers write it, and that a document looks the same on every machine that opens it."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+2"),
        Type("Layout in fixed-point units"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Every position on a page is a whole number of layout units, nine hundred and fourteen thousand four hundred to the inch. Points, millimetres and the pixels of a ninety-six dot screen are all whole numbers of them, so lines and pages break in exactly the same places on Linux, Windows, macOS and in a browser. Floating-point arithmetic, which can round differently from one machine to the next, never decides where a line ends."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Fonts travel with documents. A document carries the fonts it uses, subset where their licences ask for it, so that opening it elsewhere never reflows it into a different shape. When a family lacks a character, the character comes from the first of the family's fallbacks that has it: Arabic from Naskh, Hebrew from Noto Serif Hebrew, and Chinese from Noto Serif CJK, whose faces load only once some text needs them."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+2"),
        Type("Text in every script"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Greek, with its accents: "),
        Type("Ξεσκεπάζω την ψυχοφθόρα βδελυγμία."),
        Type(" Cyrillic, in two sentences that use every letter: "),
        Type("Съешь же ещё этих мягких французских булок, да выпей чаю. В чащах юга жил бы цитрус? Да, но фальшивый экземпляр!"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Arabic is written right to left, its letters joined: "),
        Type("نص حكيم له سر قاطع وذو شأن عظيم مكتوب على ثوب أخضر ومغلف بجلد أزرق."),
        Type(" Hebrew too, without joining, and in italic it leans as Latin does, because Noto has no Hebrew italic and xWorks slants the upright face: "),
        Key("Primary+I"),
        Type("דג סקרן שט בים מאוכזב ולפתע מצא חברה."),
        Key("Primary+I"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Chinese breaks between any two characters, except where its rules forbid it, as in the opening of the Thousand Character Classic: "),
        Key("Primary+B"),
        Type("天地玄黄，宇宙洪荒。日月盈昃，辰宿列张。寒来暑往，秋收冬藏。"),
        Key("Primary+B"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+3"),
        Type("A paragraph that reads right to left"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("مرحبا بالعالم، هذا نص عربي للاختبار. عام 2026 هو العام الذي بدأ فيه هذا المشروع، والنص هنا يبدأ من اليمين وينتهي في اليسار."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+2"),
        Type("Operations and undo"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("A document is a set of objects with identities that never change, and every edit is a small operation on them: insert text, delete text, split a paragraph, join two, set a property. Each operation knows its inverse, so undo is exact, and each can be moved over another made at the same time, so that two people editing one document arrive at the same result whichever order their edits are applied in. A transaction groups the operations of one action, and applies all of them or none."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("This session undoes everything it typed, down to an empty page, and redoes it all again. "),
        Key("Primary+B"),
        Key("Primary+I"),
        Type("What comes back is what went away, to the character."),
        Key("Primary+B"),
        Key("Primary+I"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Snapshots cost nothing. The objects live in a persistent map that shares its structure between versions, so the renderer, the spelling checker and the autosave can each hold a version of the document while the person goes on typing, and none of them ever sees half an edit."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+2"),
        Type("Pages"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("A word-processing document is a story poured into a canvas whose pages are made as they are needed, from a page style that gives their size and margins. This is the first form of that canvas, the one the word processor will grow from: later come headers and footers, footnotes, floating figures, tables that break across pages, and columns."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Where a page breaks depends only on what comes before it. Typing in the last paragraph of a long document never moves a page break near its start, so a document of five hundred pages can be laid out again from the paragraph that changed, not from the beginning, and the pages before it are drawn from what was already drawn."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("The same rule makes printing honest. What prints is a PDF made from the same display lists the screen shows, with the same fonts embedded, so a page that looks right on the screen comes out of the printer the same way, line for line."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+2"),
        Type("What comes next"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Every transaction is appended to the file as it is committed, so a crash loses nothing that was done, and closing the document and opening it again brings back its text, its formatting and its history. Then the budgets are measured on a real workstation, and the skeleton is done."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Each later track grows from these foundations rather than beside them: the spreadsheet's grid, the database's records and the modelling cube are new substrates with their own ways of addressing things, but they store their objects, record their operations, set their text and draw their pages the same way this document does."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. "),
        Key("Primary+B"),
        Type("Pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs."),
        Key("Primary+B"),
        Type(" How vexingly quick daft zebras jump! "),
        Key("Primary+I"),
        Type("Sphinx of black quartz, judge my vow."),
        Key("Primary+I"),
        // Everything undone, then everything redone: more presses than
        // there are steps, and the extra ones do nothing.
        Repeat("Primary+Z", 400),
        Expect([("Body", "")]),
        Repeat("Primary+Shift+Z", 400),
        Reopen,
    ],
    expect: [
        ("Heading 1", "A walking skeleton, typed"),
        ("Body", "This document was typed into xWorks as a person types: a key at a time, with shortcuts for its headings, its bold and its italic. Its text is stored as objects and operations, laid out in fixed-point units, shaped with HarfRust, broken into lines first fit, poured into pages of one style and drawn by the same renderer that tests use. Nothing here is hand-placed. When a paragraph does not fit at the foot of a page it breaks between lines, leaving at least two of them on each side, and a heading never ends a page without the start of the text it heads."),
        ("Body", "The aim is an office suite that is usable, fast and correct. Usable means the program does what people expect, in the order they expect it, without asking them to learn its internals. Fast means every keystroke reaches the screen before the next one, and that opening, saving and scrolling never make anyone wait for work they did not ask for. Correct means that numbers add up exactly, that text in every script is shaped and ordered as its readers write it, and that a document looks the same on every machine that opens it."),
        ("Heading 2", "Layout in fixed-point units"),
        ("Body", "Every position on a page is a whole number of layout units, nine hundred and fourteen thousand four hundred to the inch. Points, millimetres and the pixels of a ninety-six dot screen are all whole numbers of them, so lines and pages break in exactly the same places on Linux, Windows, macOS and in a browser. Floating-point arithmetic, which can round differently from one machine to the next, never decides where a line ends."),
        ("Body", "Fonts travel with documents. A document carries the fonts it uses, subset where their licences ask for it, so that opening it elsewhere never reflows it into a different shape. When a family lacks a character, the character comes from the first of the family's fallbacks that has it: Arabic from Naskh, Hebrew from Noto Serif Hebrew, and Chinese from Noto Serif CJK, whose faces load only once some text needs them."),
        ("Heading 2", "Text in every script"),
        ("Body", "Greek, with its accents: Ξεσκεπάζω την ψυχοφθόρα βδελυγμία. Cyrillic, in two sentences that use every letter: Съешь же ещё этих мягких французских булок, да выпей чаю. В чащах юга жил бы цитрус? Да, но фальшивый экземпляр!"),
        ("Body", "Arabic is written right to left, its letters joined: نص حكيم له سر قاطع وذو شأن عظيم مكتوب على ثوب أخضر ومغلف بجلد أزرق. Hebrew too, without joining, and in italic it leans as Latin does, because Noto has no Hebrew italic and xWorks slants the upright face: דג סקרן שט בים מאוכזב ולפתע מצא חברה."),
        ("Body", "Chinese breaks between any two characters, except where its rules forbid it, as in the opening of the Thousand Character Classic: 天地玄黄，宇宙洪荒。日月盈昃，辰宿列张。寒来暑往，秋收冬藏。"),
        ("Heading 3", "A paragraph that reads right to left"),
        ("Body", "مرحبا بالعالم، هذا نص عربي للاختبار. عام 2026 هو العام الذي بدأ فيه هذا المشروع، والنص هنا يبدأ من اليمين وينتهي في اليسار."),
        ("Heading 2", "Operations and undo"),
        ("Body", "A document is a set of objects with identities that never change, and every edit is a small operation on them: insert text, delete text, split a paragraph, join two, set a property. Each operation knows its inverse, so undo is exact, and each can be moved over another made at the same time, so that two people editing one document arrive at the same result whichever order their edits are applied in. A transaction groups the operations of one action, and applies all of them or none."),
        ("Body", "This session undoes everything it typed, down to an empty page, and redoes it all again. What comes back is what went away, to the character."),
        ("Body", "Snapshots cost nothing. The objects live in a persistent map that shares its structure between versions, so the renderer, the spelling checker and the autosave can each hold a version of the document while the person goes on typing, and none of them ever sees half an edit."),
        ("Heading 2", "Pages"),
        ("Body", "A word-processing document is a story poured into a canvas whose pages are made as they are needed, from a page style that gives their size and margins. This is the first form of that canvas, the one the word processor will grow from: later come headers and footers, footnotes, floating figures, tables that break across pages, and columns."),
        ("Body", "Where a page breaks depends only on what comes before it. Typing in the last paragraph of a long document never moves a page break near its start, so a document of five hundred pages can be laid out again from the paragraph that changed, not from the beginning, and the pages before it are drawn from what was already drawn."),
        ("Body", "The same rule makes printing honest. What prints is a PDF made from the same display lists the screen shows, with the same fonts embedded, so a page that looks right on the screen comes out of the printer the same way, line for line."),
        ("Heading 2", "What comes next"),
        ("Body", "Every transaction is appended to the file as it is committed, so a crash loses nothing that was done, and closing the document and opening it again brings back its text, its formatting and its history. Then the budgets are measured on a real workstation, and the skeleton is done."),
        ("Body", "Each later track grows from these foundations rather than beside them: the spreadsheet's grid, the database's records and the modelling cube are new substrates with their own ways of addressing things, but they store their objects, record their operations, set their text and draw their pages the same way this document does."),
        ("Body", "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. Pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs. How vexingly quick daft zebras jump! Sphinx of black quartz, judge my vow."),
    ],
    marks: [
        ("Nothing here is hand-placed.", ["italic"]),
        ("usable, fast and correct", ["bold"]),
        ("דג סקרן שט בים מאוכזב ולפתע מצא חברה.", ["italic"]),
        ("天地玄黄，宇宙洪荒。日月盈昃，辰宿列张。寒来暑往，秋收冬藏。", ["bold"]),
        ("What comes back is what went away, to the character.", ["bold", "italic"]),
        ("Pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs.", ["bold"]),
        ("Sphinx of black quartz, judge my vow.", ["italic"]),
    ],
    status: Some("Page 1 of 3   ·   Heading 1   ·   20 pt   ·   968 words"),
)
